 "_comment": "Tier numerals I-VII (R7): the plain diamonds (top row) for every card, list and odds cell, and the fleur diamonds (second row) for the one large badge a screen shows -- the selected soldier, the reroll panel's tier. Plain: an opaque cut to the rhombus through the gold rim's four tips (centres measured on the rim, half-width 60, half-height 69), so a badge sits in the same place on every card; its dark slate face is ground-dark and must not be keyed. Fleur: keyed off the ground for the ornament ('floor' clears the ground's grain) with the face held opaque by 'solid'; the side fleurs of neighbours meet, so each is cut at the midpoint between centres, and 2 px lower than the tips' midline so the badge's solid body, not its fleur tips, is centred in the box. Both drawn down to the largest size a screen uses (50x50, 80x124). The reputation hexes further down the sheet are cut by numerals_rep.json.",
